WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.049
I grew up in a small village.

00:00:12.049 --> 00:00:12.946
That's why I think America is too big for me.

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:35.690
There are a lot of families in Iran that are not like my family

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:39.010
when the compulsory hijab was applied on women

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:44.109
some families started to cry for their daughters.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:04.360
As a kid my brother was an example of freedom
freedom--was a symbol of freedom that

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:08.330
I didn't have.  How was free to run

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:11.920
in a green, lovely farm;

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:15.320
how was free to ride a bicycle in a nice

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:18.159
village... my village is the best!

00:01:18.159 --> 00:01:20.159
Just look at them.

00:01:20.159 --> 00:01:22.659
I love that

00:01:22.659 --> 00:01:26.380
Two women with head scarves, and two women without head scarves.

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:30.200
look at how they are free. They just, you know, walk past each other

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:35.280
without judging each other. Without getting arrested by the morality police.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:40.290
Isn't that beautiful? I want to see this in my own country.

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:44.580
I started to publish this one: It's me, and me.

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:51.630
So that's why people started to send their pictures and I ask women to

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:56.390
sharing experiences which they did.

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:15.020
Women who take pictures of themselves, outside, in Iran

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:18.360
without their headscarves
which is a punishable crime.

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:24.840
every individual
story makes me really happy

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:32.549
there are a lot of women sending their
pictures

00:02:32.549 --> 00:02:38.689
holding a sign saying that "we believe in hijab, but we hate compulsory hijab"

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:41.880
Some of the pictures come from those

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:48.980
young girls saying that they just want to feel the wind in their hair. It's a simple demand.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:53.880
Like this. It's forbidden. To be like this is forbidden in Iran.

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:59.370
They take off their scarf in front of these signs.

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:05.040
This is the "Proper Islamic Hijab"

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:09.370
There are a lot of pictures that you can see men supporting women.

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:12.830
All the women in my family, they wear hijab.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:15.400
This is not a black and white issue.

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:20.020
All families in Iran are not like my family. There are so many families in Iran

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:21.320
who do not believe in compulsory hijab.

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:28.160
Iran is for all Iranians. You cannot just hide one side of Iran and say "this is Iran"

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:29.900
This is a lie!

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:32.380
Iran is me and my mother.

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:36.320
my mother wants to wear a scarf. I do not want to wear a scarf.

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:41.020
Iran should be for both of us.

